# ==============================================================================
# KingOfFate .gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# This file used to be the standard GitHub Python template (200+ lines). Most of
# it described packaging, CI and coverage workflows this project does not have,
# and a few of its rules were actively dangerous here:
#
#   lib/          would have silently ignored a tools/lib/ directory
#   build/        would have ignored any directory named build
#   .coverage     and friends: noise, since there is no Python test runner
#
# What remains is what actually applies: bytecode, virtual environments, and the
# project's own local-output rules below.
#
# If you add a tool, run `git check-ignore -v <path>` before assuming it will be
# committed -- that is how the lib/ trap was found.

# Byte-compiled / optimised Python files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Compiled extensions
*.so

# Local logs that turn up outside logs/ (the engine writes its own under
# engine/ikemen-go/save/, which is ignored with the rest of the runtime output).
*.log

# ==============================================================================
# KingOfFate project additions
# ==============================================================================

# Local logs (build / runtime evidence). The directory is kept, raw logs are local only.
/logs/*
!/logs/.gitkeep
!/logs/build/
!/logs/build/**

# Local runtime distribution assembled for testing / release packaging.
/dist/*
!/dist/.gitkeep

# Build temporaries (see scripts/build_engine.ps1 - some environments deny native
# compilers write access to the system temp directory).
/.tmp/

# Local assistant/tooling state. Not part of the project deliverable; the directory
# itself is kept on disk by the tooling, it is just never published.
/.workbuddy/

# Engine build outputs. These live inside the engine submodule (which already
# ignores them) - repeated here so they can never be committed by accident.
engine/ikemen-go/Ikemen_GO.exe
engine/ikemen-go/Ikemen_GO_x86.exe
engine/ikemen-go/lib/
engine/ikemen-go/build/screenpack/
engine/ikemen-go/save/
engine/ikemen-go/debug/
engine/ikemen-go/video/

# Locally built executables. Only the optional engine-decoder cross-check builds
# one, next to its source under tests/tools/xcheck_engine_decoder/.
*.exe
